{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":205073,"duration_api_ms":203964,"num_turns":25,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"927e2f0d-1944-4687-a079-f056e8d0559a","total_cost_usd":1.18644375,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87971,"cache_read_input_tokens":898810,"output_tokens":7486,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":87971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":7486,"cacheReadInputTokens":898810,"cacheCreationInputTokens":87971,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.18644375,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[],"summary":"Reviewed all key implementation files end-to-end: water.rs (concentration helpers + ConcentrationView), state.rs (TankState facade methods + volume/areal helpers), geometry.rs (volume computation), and all consumer systems (nitrogen_cycle.rs, plant_growth.rs, algae_growth.rs, dissolved_oxygen.rs, shrimp.rs, chemistry.rs, microfauna.rs, snapshot.rs). Also reviewed budget.rs, process.rs (legacy shims), and the full concentration_helpers.rs test suite including proptest.\n\n**Correctness**: All required helpers are implemented (TAN, nitrite, nitrate, DOC, DIC, DO, phosphate, alkalinity, plus extras: DON, calcium, magnesium, GH, KH, TDS, conductivity). The canonical `concentration_from_total` function correctly guards against NaN, infinity, zero/near-zero volume, and negative totals. All process systems have been migrated to use either `state.concentrations()` (ConcentrationView) or the TankState facade methods. The remaining direct total/volume divisions in nitrogen_cycle.rs (detritus densities), microfauna.rs (detritus/periphyton densities), and chemistry.rs (`compute_ph_from_totals` taking totals as explicit params) are all legitimate — they operate on non-water-chemistry quantities or have deliberate API signatures.\n\n**Safety**: Helpers never return negative values (enforced by `.max(0.0)` in `concentration_from_total` and in derived helpers like `gh_d`, `kh_d`). The proptest covers all helpers with randomized geometry and water chemistry inputs from 0 to 1e6, verifying non-negativity. Zero-volume edge cases (full substrate displacement, zero fill height, empty substrate) are tested deterministically.\n\n**Architecture**: The three-layer design (WaterState helpers taking explicit volume_l, ConcentrationView with pre-captured volume, TankState facade methods) is clean. snapshot.rs consolidation is complete — it now uses `state.concentrations()` instead of ad hoc division. The `legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l` shim for half-saturation parameters is well-documented as a migration bridge to a fixed 20L reference volume. No duplicate concentration logic remains.\n\n**Tests**: 10 tests covering canonical values, zero-volume variants, large tanks, areal density, constructor round-trips, ConcentrationView/TankState agreement, and seeded-example consistency. The proptest covers all 19+ output helpers. All tests pass; clippy is clean with no warnings.\n\nNo bugs, safety problems, or significant maintainability risks found."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"04a1fd02-60cb-4394-810e-2a9590a26c6f"}
